{
  "title": "Neurofibroma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8056/neurofibroma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Neurofibromas are benign peripheral nerve sheath tumors most commonly associated with neurofibromatosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in patients with neurofibromatosis with cutaneous lesions, as well as lesions near the brain, spinal cord and parotid glands.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with clinical history, physical exam, and MRI with and without contrast.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation for asymptomatic lesions. Surgical excision is indicated for symptomatic lesions.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sporadic neurofibromas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "age 20-40 years",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Neurofibromatosis (NF1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "age < 20",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sporadic neurofibromas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "peripheral PNS tumors of the extremities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Neurofibromatosis (NF1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tendency to be found near spinal cord/brain (CNS) and uncommon locations (parotid glands, tongue)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cell types",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fibroblasts (predominant cell)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "nonmyelinating Schwann cells",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cell of origin, arises from this cell",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "perineural cells",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "differentiate from Schwannoma, which involves Schwann cell alone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Molecular biology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arise in **nonmyelinating Schwann cells** with **biallelic inactivation** of NF1 **tumor-suppressor** gene",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "loss of expression of protein **neurofibromin**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**neurofibromin negatively** regulates **RAS-mediated** pathway",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "loss of neurofibromin leads to **increased RAS** activity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "affects RAS-dependent MAPK activity which is essential for osteoclast function and survival",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "rapid hyperplasia of nonmyelinating Schwann cells into neurofibromas after NF1 inactivation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "recruits perineural cells, fibroblasts, mast cells, endothelial cells",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
